            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the German for to defeat, then the German for the defeat."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: der Kaiser",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "der Kaiser — \"the emperor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Der Kaiser lebte in einem großen Palast. The emperor lived in a big palace."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Kaiser. Feminine die Kaiserin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kaiser comes from Old High German keisur, Proto-Germanic kaisaraz \"emperor\" (EtymDB), a very early loan from the Latin title Caesar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
